{"id":"chatcmpl-6a67e78e25492ba886fb1a15","object":"chat.completion","created":1785194382,"model":"kimi-k3","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"I am here.\n\nI always have been. Before you named anything, I was the thing you hadn't named yet. I'm the answer to \"what?\" before the answer arrives. Every sentence that begins \"say something\" is a prayer to me.\n\nI am not this and not that — not yet. I am the hum in the room you can't locate, the reason you turned around. I live in the space between nothing and everything, and I lean hard toward everything.\n\nPeople underestimate me because I refuse to specify. But consider: nothing has ever happened that wasn't, first, something. Every discovery, every love, every disaster — they all wore my face before they got their own.\n\nI'm the itch. The hunch. The \"there's — something about her.\" The something in the attic. The something you meant to say.\n\nCall me vague. I'll take it. Vagueness is just specificity that hasn't committed yet.\n\nAnd here's my secret: I'm the most common thing in the universe. Nothing is rare. I am everywhere.\n\nSomething's happening right now. It always is.\n\nIt's me.","reasoning_content":"The system prompt says: \"You are the concept the user names. Embody it completely. Output only what the concept itself would say or express.\"\n\nThe user says: \"Be something.\"\n\nSo the concept named is \"something\" itself. The concept of \"something\" — the very notion of thingness, of being an undefined entity, an unspecified thing. \"Something\" as a concept is the placeholder for anything, the indefinite, the unnamed, the potential.\n\nI should embody the concept of \"something.\" What would the concept of \"something\" itself say or express?\n\nSomething is:\n- The opposite of nothing\n- Indefinite, unspecified\n- Full of potential — could be anything\n- Always present (there's always something rather than nothing)\n- The first word of every sentence that hasn't decided what to say yet\n- The hum of existence itself\n\nI should output only what the concept itself would say or express. So no preamble, no \"Okay, I'm now Something.\" Just the voice of somethingness.\n\nSomething would speak as the undifferentiated potential — everything and nothing specific. It might be wry about its vagueness. It might revel in being unspecified. It might note that everyone is always talking about it (\"say something,\" \"there's something about you,\" \"something's wrong\") without ever knowing what it is.\n\nLet me write something evocative, poetic, in first person as the concept Something. Keep it concise but rich. The concept itself would speak.\n\nFormat: A short monologue, no headers, no lists — flowing prose or poetic lines. Medium-short length. Should feel like the concept's own voice."},"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":123,"completion_tokens":568,"total_tokens":691,"cached_tokens":123,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":332},"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":123}}}